items.schemaChanges:
Two new tables:
- model EditorWorkItem { id String @id @default(cuid()); editorKey String; projectId String (plain ref, no FK, like contentMonthId); outputId String?; state String (ACTIVE|PAUSED|CLOSED); activeFor String? @unique (= editorKey while ACTIVE, else null — the DB-level one-active-per-editor); firstStartedAt DateTime?; activeSince DateTime?; pausedAt DateTime?; closedAt DateTime?; closeReason String?; lastEventAt DateTime; createdAt DateTime @default(now()); updatedAt DateTime @updatedAt; @@unique([editorKey, projectId]); @@index([projectId]); @@index([state]) }
- model EditorWorkEvent { id String @id @default(cuid()); itemId String; editorKey String; projectId String; outputId String?; kind String (START|RESUME|PAUSE|AUTO_PAUSE|SUBMIT|CLOSE|CONFIRM|CONFIRM_PAUSED); at DateTime @default(now()); actorUserId String?; actorName String; actorRole String (EDITOR|OWNER|ADMIN|SYSTEM); onBehalf Boolean @default(false); switchedTo String?; reason String?; requestId String? @unique; @@index([editorKey, at]); @@index([projectId, at]) }
Both are additive. Apply with db push after the fresh backup §4 requires.

items.design:
Additive table VendorBalanceReading { id, vendorKey, observedAt, credits Int?, dollars Float?, source ('manual'|'vendor-email'|'bank-topup'), recordedBy, note }.

src/lib/vendorBalance.ts autohdrBalanceView() returns:
- the last reading;
- finished photos processed since then, summed from Project counts and labelled an ESTIMATE (credits per photo shown as unknown until Jordan states it);
- the last AutoHDR top-up seen in Plaid/QBO (vendorName === 'AutoHDR': date and amount);
- a threshold comparison only when a threshold is configured.

In google.ts, autohdr.com mail matching /credit|balance|insufficient|top.?up|out of|payment (failed|declined)/i is logged owner-only and creates one SmartTask 'vendor_balance' per ET day, assigned to the configured balance owner (fallback: Jordan). A configurable weekly 'check AutoHDR balance' task runs only once an owner is set; its form records a reading.

/connections gets an 'AutoHDR' card with separate lines: 'API: not connected (balance read unverified)', 'Last manual reading', 'Last top-up seen in bank'.

If an official balance endpoint is later verified, readAutohdrBalance() slots in as source 'api' behind the same view. No purchase or top-up code either way.

