items.correction:
The gap is narrower than 'no concurrency proof'. PGlite already proves these at statement granularity:
- single-statement compare-and-set claims (cp02-revision-policy §8, approve vs request, 10/10);
- unique-key dedupe;
- lease reclaim after a SIGKILL (cron-route-journey §5).

Only a real Postgres can show:
- overlapping interactive transactions and contended advisory locks;
- Prisma upserts that are not native, interleaving inside their transaction;
- pool and transaction timeouts (P2024/P2028; defaults maxWait 2 s, timeout 5 s) at a Vercel-sized pool;
- cross-process interleaving.

A Neon branch is not needed. It is an account action and would copy real client data.

